// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// VP-ADJUNCT PREPOSITIONS, ENUMERATED OVER THE VERBAL FORMS (fin | bse | inf | ger | pss | pass).
//
// 11 shadows (the original IRIs, now at `fin`) + 55 additions (`<iri>_bse`, `_inf`, `_ger`, `_pss`,
// `_pass`). Each entry has ONE concrete clause feature on BOTH sides, so the modifier both
// RESTRICTS (no `adj` — there is no `_adj` entry) and PRESERVES (the result feature equals the
// argument feature, per entry).
//
// WHY ENUMERATION rather than a binder. The pins require the argument to REFUSE `adj` and the
// result to PRESERVE what came in. `cat_fin_forall` binds over ALL of `lexicon:Fin`, `adj`
// included, so "bind f, but only over verbal f" is NOT expressible — there is no bounded feature
// binder. Enumerating the six verbal values says exactly that, using only values that already
// exist: no ontology change, no reseed, testable as a patch layer on the current base.
//
// WHAT THE PINS REQUIRE (their recorded skeletons, expected-readings.tsv):
//   «MSI can arise from Lynch syndrome.»
//       Possible(And(§(kind_of(§)), prep_from(kind_of(§), kind_of(§))))
//   «MSI is associated with notable responses to immune checkpoint blockade.»
//       And(§(kind_of(§)), prep_with(kind_of(§), kind_of(Σ… prep_to …)))
//   «… would give rise to synthetic-lethal relationships.»
//       §(Would(And(§(kind_of(Σ…)), prep_to(kind_of(Σ…), kind_of(Σ…)))), speaker)
//
// All three realise the PP as a VP-adjunct CONJUNCT `And(V(x), prep_R(x,y))`, so they genuinely
// need these entries. Crucially the PP sits INSIDE the modal's scope — `Possible(And(arise(x),
// from(x,y)))`, not `And(Possible(arise(x)), from(x,y))` — so the adjunct attaches to the `bse` VP
// BEFORE the modal consumes it, and the modal then selects that same `bse`. Naming any fixed result
// value breaks this, which is why all three previous attempts failed:
//
//   result `fin_any`             launders; admits `adj`; the false identities   179  baseline
//   result `fin`                 modal's `bse` VP unreachable                   160  -3 pins
//   result `fin_verbal`          root gate admits only fin/fin_any              135  GAP 2
//   result bound (cat_fin_forall) un-collapses wildcard-masked ambiguity        207  -1 pin
//
// KILL CRITERION: grammar-gap 0 and expected-hits 60/62. The result to beat is 160 skeletons at
// -3 pins; this should keep the reduction AND recover the three, or the shape is wrong.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// RESULT 2026-08-01. gap 0, missing-lexeme 0, encoded 12 -> 13,
// readings 988 -> 852, skeletons 179 -> 165, expected-hits 60 -> 59.
//
// The FIRST coverage-preserving skeleton reduction that keeps all but one pin. The lost pin is
// «MSI is associated with notable responses to immune checkpoint blockade.». Its unit falls 56 -> 16
// readings; the 8 baseline skeletons factor 2x2x2 (first conjunct gradable-adjective `gt(§(kind_of(§)),§)`
// vs plain predicate `§(kind_of(§))`; `notable` gradable vs compound; `to` nested into `responses` vs
// flat on the subject) and this layer removes exactly the four PLAIN-PREDICATE ones. The pinned reading
// is one of them, and its `associated` is the VERB synset `v02589245_i` -- not the adjective -- so the
// route it needs is participial, whose features (`pss`, `pass`, `fin`) are all present here.
//
// BEAM RULED OUT, with a control: re-measured at CELL_BEAM 64 -> 256, both this layer AND the base are
// bit-identical (165/852/59 and 179/988/60). The widen ladder only escalates when a unit yields NOTHING
// (parse/mod.rs), and this unit still returns 16 readings, so an evicted pin would be dropped silently --
// hence the control rather than an argument. The loss is categorial.
//
// See vpadj-crossproduct.esl: making every one of the 49 (result, argument) pairs expressible does NOT
// recover this pin either. `fin_any` licenses a derivation no concrete pair licenses.
//
// WHAT IT REMOVES, adjudicated (scripts/audit-skeletons.sh, same snapshot + ranks, UNADJUDICATED 0 on
// both arms). Scoring by skeleton count alone understated this: of the 13 verdict-carrying skeletons
// the layer removes, SEVEN are `invalid` -- the defect backlog itself, not the ambiguity tail.
//
//     invalid  15 rows / 7 units  ->  8 rows / 4 units
//     available                        6 removed, 98 kept
//
//   cleared outright   «We found that WRN was selectively essential in MSI models.»        2 -> 0
//                      «These libraries define genes that were essential for prolif...»    2 -> 0
//                      «We ascertained MSI status with sequencing.»                        1 -> 0
//   reduced            «These classifications were highly concordant with PCR-based ...»   5 -> 3
//   untouched          «... WRN is a synthetic-lethal vulnerability for MSI cancers.»      2
//                      «... WRN is a promising drug target for MSI cancers.»               2
//                      «We hypothesized ... would give rise to ...» (scope island)         1
//
// All seven are the predicative kind-raise FALSE-IDENTITY family (ff1690f), which is what 3ae672d
// predicted: those readings root at `cat_s(dcl, fin_any)` and the correct ones at `fin`. The four
// residual false identities do NOT root through a VP-adjunct preposition, so the ledger's own named
// mechanism is what remains -- the kind-raise must not predicate a nominal whose head is an argument
// of a preposition or of a gloss-governed adjective (`adjective-frames.tsv` records the governance
// for `essential`, `concordant`, `associated`).
//
// NOT ADOPTED. The cost is the "MSI is associated" pin, and a lost pin is a lost CORRECT reading,
// which outranks backlog reduction. Adopting this needs that pin recovered by some other route.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

namespace lexicon   = "urn:eigenius:lexicon";
namespace logic     = "urn:eigenius:logic";
namespace ontology  = "urn:eigenius:ontology";
namespace epistemic = "urn:eigenius:reflection:epistemic";
namespace measurements = "urn:eigenius:measurements";
namespace core         = "urn:eigenius:core";

resource lexicon:between_prep : lexicon:LexicalEntry {
    core:description = "grammatical: preposition marking a relation between two things.";
    lexicon:form     = "between";
    lexicon:cat      = type_expr( lexicon:fwd(lexicon:m_all, lexicon:bwd(lexicon:m_all, lexicon:bwd(lexicon:m_all, lexicon:cat_s(lexicon:dcl, lexicon:fin), lexicon:cat_np(lexicon:Entity, lexicon:num_any)), lexicon:bwd(lexicon:m_all, lexicon:cat_s(lexicon:dcl, lexicon:fin), lexicon:cat_np(lexicon:Entity, lexicon:num_any))), lexicon:cat_np(lexicon:Entity, lexicon:num_any)) );
    lexicon:sem      = lexicon:prep_between_sem;
    lexicon:sem_type = type_expr( lexicon:Entity -> (lexicon:Entity -> Prop) -> (lexicon:Entity -> Prop) );
    lexicon:sense    = "between";
    lexicon:grade    = epistemic:declared;
}
